SERVER IN BACKEND (NODE + EXPRESS)

The server file is the entry point of the backend application.
It starts the server and connects all parts together.

--------------------------------
What Server File Contains
--------------------------------

1) Server Initialization
- Creates Express app
- Defines server port

--------------------------------
2) Middleware Registration
- JSON parser
- CORS
- Custom middleware

--------------------------------
3) Route Registration
- Connects routes with app
- Example:
  • app.use("/api/auth", authRoutes)

--------------------------------
4) Database Connection
- Connects backend to database
- Runs before server starts

--------------------------------
5) Error Handling Setup
- Global error middleware
- Handles unexpected errors

--------------------------------
6) Server Listener
- Starts server using listen()
- Makes backend available to clients

--------------------------------
Server Flow
--------------------------------

Start Server
     ↓
Load Middleware
     ↓
Load Routes
     ↓
Wait for Requests
     ↓
Send Responses

--------------------------------
Why Server File is Important
--------------------------------

• Central control of backend
• Connects all components
• Required to run application
• Entry point of project

--------------------------------
Project Structure Example
--------------------------------

backend/
│── server.js
│── routes/
│── controllers/
│── models/
│── middleware/

